DESCRIPTION:Brain Brew Ride / Krishna BhattSpend a Sunday exploring the br
 ain\, sharing a meal and connecting with your neighbors at Brain Brew Comm
 unity Day—a free\, family-friendly event at Buchanan YMCA.\nJoin us on S
 unday\, October 18\, 2026\, from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m. for hands-on brain-them
 ed activities\, “Brain Olympics” games\, local coffee sampling and lun
 ch. Visit the memory wall\, learn about brain health and enjoy time with f
 amily\, friends and neighbors.\nOrganized by high school students Krishna 
 Bhatt and Govind Krishnan\, Brain Brew brings generations together to rais
 e awareness of Alzheimer’s and Parkinson’s. Families\, older adults\, 
 students and care partners are welcome.\n\nAdmission is free\, and lunch i
 s included. Donations are optional (through recommended\, ~$25) and suppor
 t the Alzheimer’s Association and Michael J. Fox Foundation.\nWhen: Sund
 ay\, October 18\, 2026\, 10 a.m.–3 p.m.\nWhere: Buchanan YMCA\, 1530 Buc
 hanan Street\, San Francisco\nRSVP: https://forms.gle/TBYodKPwEr8REew2A\nQ
 uestions: krishbhatt2019@gmail.com\nThis listing is for the October 18 Com
 munity Day. The October 17 ride and October 24 Walk mentioned on the flyer
  are separate activities.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://brainbrewsf.org\nDet
 ails: https://sf.funcheap.com/free-brain-brew-community-day-brain-games-lu
 nch-coffee-sf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
